    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Clin Use: alternative for PCN-allergic pts across most guidelines; IDSA also lists doxycycline as a general alternative to amoxicillin-clavulanate for any adult w/ acute bacterial rhinosinusitis"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Also: MRSA coverage (cellulitis: TMP-SMX, doxycycline, clindamycin); tick-borne dz (Lyme: doxycycline, amoxicillin, cefuroxime; RMSF: doxycycline, chloramphenicol); syphilis (doxycycline, tetracycline = alternatives); acne (doxycycline + minocycline = MC oral abx; doxycycline over azithromycin); blepharitis (oral tetracyclines reserved for severe, refractory cases)"
     }
    ]
   },
